<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bandiagara</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bandiagara is a town in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a> on the plateau above the Bandiagara Escarpment, the line of cliffs inhabited by the Dogon people and listed as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>. After the death of Umar Tall in 1864, his nephew Tidiani Tall made it the capital of the eastern part of the Toucouleur Empire. French forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-archinard">Louis Archinard</a> took it in 1893.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bandiagara.jpg" alt="Bandiagara" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: upyernoz from Haverford, USA · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bandiagara_(6459419).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
